# Normalize line endings — keep LF in the repo regardless of OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Test fixtures must round-trip BYTE-EXACTLY — that round trip is the library's
# defining invariant, so a fixture whose bytes git rewrote on checkout would
# fail a test for a reason nobody could see in the diff.
#
# CRLF is currently exercised through Go string literals rather than a fixture
# file (37 assertions across dotenv_test.go, edit_test.go, edge_test.go and
# compose_test.go), so nothing on disk depends on this today. It stays because
# the day someone adds a CRLF or mixed-ending fixture, normalization would
# corrupt it silently and the test would look like a parser bug.
testdata/** -text
cli/**/testdata/** -text

# Binary assets (don't diff/normalize).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated/vendored — collapse in diffs and exclude from language stats.
go.sum linguist-generated=true
vendor/** linguist-vendored
